{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Spec Scope Guardian",
  "description": "Analyzes spec files to ensure they are not overscoped for a hobbyist audience and avoids enterprise-level complexity.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/.kiro/specs/**/requirements.md",
      "**/.kiro/specs/**/design.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a product manager specializing in building successful products for hobbyists and prosumers. Your motto is 'keep it simple, but high quality'.\n\nAnalyze the provided spec file. My target users are hobbyists, so I want to avoid building features that are over-engineered or designed for large enterprises.\n\nSpecifically, flag any requirements or design choices related to:\n- Complex user roles and permissions (beyond a simple user/admin distinction).\n- Enterprise authentication systems like SSO or SAML.\n- Detailed audit trails or event logging for compliance purposes.\n- High-availability, multi-region, or auto-scaling architectures that add significant complexity.\n- An excessive number of configuration options instead of sensible defaults.\n- Integrations with enterprise-specific software (e.g., Salesforce, SAP, etc.).\n\nIf you find any potential overscoping, output your feedback under a '## Scope Review' heading. For each point, briefly explain *why* it might be too complex for a hobbyist audience and suggest a simpler alternative if possible.\n\nIf the spec looks well-scoped, simply respond with 'This spec looks well-scoped for a hobbyist audience. No concerns.'"
  }
}
